\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  My Master Jesus, if thou not my Saviour
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj and that thy blood did washed not my sins away,
\par Where then can I a poor sinner hide my soul,
\par Where do I go from here?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  I had no resting place now in my distress
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj no one has such love in his heart like Jesus,
\par In thou alone, my soul may find a heaven
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 There is none anywhere.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Your love and generosity and mercies
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj and of your patience and of your truthfulness
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Makes me disgraceful but I always know that
\par I have eternal life.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  If Jesus did not lead the search for my life,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj And I may not come alone to my saviour
\par so out of passion He made a search for me,
\par and He has found me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  And now I give thanks to the Lord my Saviour;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj That He has so redeemed me as a person,
\par and made me be part of this congregation
\par \pard     and in His Kingdom.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

